commenti.body:
Medium Cool (1969) ends at the actual 1968 Democratic National Convention protests. The filmmaker, Haskell Wexler, is a renowned cinematographer. The film uses a cinéma vérité style while having a fully fictional story set in the nonfictional space and time of Chicago 1968. It takes a Nightcrawler-like character and thrusts him in to the politics of the time.

&#x200B;

There is a documentary called Look Out Haskell, It's Real! about the making of as well.
